<title>UK: World Bank adds 100 bln lire to 10-yr hybrid bond. [CORRECTED 16:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>World Bank adds 100 bln lire to 10-yr hybrid bond. [CORRECTED 16:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following structured bond has been increased to 600 billion lire from 500 billion lire, joint lead managers Credito Italiano and Citibank said Wednesday. (Corrects from &quot;has been increased to 500 billion lire from 400 billion lire&quot; to make clear the size of the bond.)</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT  **100 BLN LIRE  COUPON    *9.50	MATURITY   *27.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.20    PAY DATE    27.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ   *ANNUAL</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES     *CALL AT PAR THREE YEARS AFTER WHICH NOTES PAY</p>
<p>		19.50 MINUS TWO TIMES SIX-MONTH LIBOR.</p>
<p>	    **BRINGS TOTAL SIZE TO 600 BILLION LIRE.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
